<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch credit insurer NCM in Oman LNG plant deal.</title>
<headline>Dutch credit insurer NCM in Oman LNG plant deal.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch credit insurer Nederlandsche Credietverzekering Maatschappij NV (NCM) said on Friday it would insure the Dutch part of building and operating a large-scale liquified natural gas (LNG) plant in Oman.</p>
<p>The plant, which will have annual production capacity of 6.6 million tonnes of LNG, requires a total investment of more than five billion guilders. The Dutch part of the investment will be about 500 million guilders, NCM said in a statement.</p>
<p>The major participants in the project are the Oman government and Shell Overseas Trading Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
